# A search by === through a list of which nothing is known. The loop tells a list from bytes in front. Its list had one copy, which read every element boxed out of whatever storage, and every
# fraction took the rare way of the comparison: 27 instructions an element. Now the list is first asked for storage of numbers, as where a loop reckons with its elements: that copy reads raw: 7.
# A list that fails the question goes on to the copy for lists of anything: a guess that fails costs one test. And the needle counts as a number not only where it is written: an operator on bits
# has made it. Where the needle is a parameter of which nothing is known (findGiven) nothing is asked, as before.
# f1 = find, f2 = findGiven
